# The calibration panel and its rail button.

#. The rail row that summarises calibration and opens the panel.
msgid "calib.button.label"
msgstr "calibration"

msgid "calib.button.working"
msgstr "calibration   working…"

msgid "calib.button.complete"
msgstr "calibration   complete"

#. {have} of {total} products exist. A count rather than a list: the rail
#. is 258 px wide and a truncated list looks like information and is not.
msgid "calib.button.progress"
msgstr "calibration   {have} of {total}"

msgid "calib.button.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Dark, flat, white balance and preview profile for this configuration.\n"
"Click to open. Missing products are a nag, not a gate. Capture anyway\n"
"and the file records what it did and did not have."

#. The dark frame.
msgid "calib.dark.label"
msgstr "dark"

msgid "calib.dark.action"
msgstr "Shoot"

msgid "calib.dark.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Cap the lens or switch the lamp off, then shoot.\n"
"Averaged over several frames; ages after about eight hours because this "
"sensor has no cooling."

#. The flat field. Two jobs, so two buttons: gather blank fields, then
#. combine them.
msgid "calib.flat.label"
msgstr "flat"

msgid "calib.flat.action.bank"
msgstr "Bank"

msgid "calib.flat.action.build"
msgstr "Build"

msgid "calib.flat.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Set the light and the optics the way you will shoot, find blank glass\n"
"and press Bank. Move the stage a little and press it again, four times\n"
"in all.\n"
"\n"
"The glass does not need to be clean. The frames are medianed, so\n"
"debris on the slide lands somewhere different each time and drops out,\n"
"while the illumination falloff and any dust on the sensor stay put and\n"
"are corrected. That only works if the stage actually moves between\n"
"presses. Defocusing slightly helps too.\n"
"\n"
"Each press freezes the preview for about a second, and a flat is only\n"
"valid at the illumination it was shot under."

msgid "calib.flat.build.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Combine the banked fields into a flat, and measure the white balance\n"
"from it. Needs at least two, and rejects debris properly from three."

#. Shown before anything has been banked.
msgid "calib.flat.detail.how"
msgstr "blank glass, then Bank"

#. {banked} of {wanted} blank fields gathered so far.
msgid "calib.flat.detail.count"
msgstr "{banked}/{wanted}  move a little between each"

#. Fewer than three will not median away debris on the glass.
msgid "calib.flat.detail.debris"
msgstr "{banked}/{wanted}  3+ rejects debris"

msgid "calib.flat.detail.ready"
msgstr "{banked}/{wanted}  ready to build"

#. Said after banking without having moved the stage.
msgid "calib.flat.warn.same_patch"
msgstr "the view has not moved -- debris in this field will survive the median"

#. White balance, which is derived rather than shot.
msgid "calib.wb.label"
msgstr "white balance"

msgid "calib.wb.action"
msgstr "-"

msgid "calib.wb.detail"
msgstr "from flat"

msgid "calib.wb.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Measured from the flat. A featureless illuminated field is neutral by "
"definition."

#. The preview profile: what the ISP does to the sensor data.
msgid "calib.lut.label"
msgstr "preview profile"

msgid "calib.lut.action"
msgstr "Profile"

msgid "calib.lut.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Measures what the ISP does to the sensor data, so the histogram can "
"report real headroom.\nTakes an exposure ramp, so it needs a few seconds."
